2026-10-18T18:16:22.3896398Z [36;1m# --no-renames, and it is not cosmetic: a rename is reported by its[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3896675Z [36;1m# DESTINATION only, so moving CLAUDE.md to RENAMED.md yields a list[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3896953Z [36;1m# matching no glob and the approval gate would not fire on the change[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3897247Z [36;1m# that removed a policy file. Measured both ways before wiring it.[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3897538Z [36;1mgit diff --no-renames --name-only "$PR_BASE...$PR_HEAD" > /tmp/pr-files.txt[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3897780Z [36;1mwc -l < /tmp/pr-files.txt[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3897981Z [36;1m# The same diff less its additions: what the base already had. A[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3898244Z [36;1m# reporter that grades `main` is exempt from `## Red checks` only[0m
2026-10-18T18:16:22.3898705Z [36;1m# while the diff touches none of its inputs, and a delivery row the[0m
